<!--
  A stipulation, not a filing. Nothing here was measured. The figures exist to put one state
  of the model in front of a checker, and that state is an unmeasured conversion.

  `asrt:Part/factor` is optional, and a `pm:StatedFactor` has three branches, so a part files
  one of four states:

    no `factor` element   the part is already in the composed unit, and converts by exactly one
    `factor/claim`        a stated conversion, at the filed rate
    `factor/derivation`   a conversion the receiver computes from a named identity
    `factor/absent`       somebody looked and could not size it                  this file

  A conversion nobody has measured is an `unmeasured` absence inside the factor, a different
  document from a part with no `factor` at all.

  Reading this one as a factor of one is the failure: it asserts a rate nobody filed, and the
  fused figure would look perfectly ordinary. `composition/converted.sqlc` converts by one only
  where the element is left out, and drops a part whose factor is a typed blank;
  `composition/unsized_conversions.sqlc` suspends the sum of a fusion with such a part, as an
  unsized elimination does.

    team-a nameplate   10 shifts per week     already in the composed unit, no `factor`
    team-b nameplate   10 turnos por semana   a conversion nobody measured
    fused nameplate    17, the composer's     the parts' sum cannot be computed, and it is
                       own figure             not 20

  The eliminations below are filed `unmeasured` as well, so the sum is also suspended on a
  ground the model recognises for any fusion, and the factor state stays the one new thing
  here. A fixture shows that a state can be reached, never that a reading of it is correct.
-->
